GFOpenTorrent: libpico and its HTTP client without Windows.
AmigaOS has no DLLs: IPlugin::Load gives no plugin (Application only
looks for Plugin*.dll), and the plugin C API stays as it is with the
module as its init function. http/httpclient.hpp declares the client on
the toolkit's wxWebRequest (compat/picotorrent/httpclient_amiga.cpp, which
the build copies over httpclient.cpp; WinHTTP's code stays for Windows).
libpico_mainwnd_native_handle gives the toolkit's handle. Each change
sits under __WXOPENLAYOUT__, Windows' code as it was.
